  "nl_text": "This schema is for a CMS called Refinery, which is a Ruby on Rails application. It has 12 tables, each representing a different entity or aspect of the CMS.\nThe first table, `refinery_authentication_devise_roles`, stores information about user roles. Each row represents a role, with columns for the role's ID, title, and other relevant data.\nThe second table, `refinery_authentication_devise_users`, stores information about individual users. Each row represents a user, with columns for the user's ID, username, email, encrypted password, and other relevant data.\nThe third table, `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users`, stores information about which users belong to which roles. Each row represents a user-role relationship, with columns for the user's ID and the role's ID.\nThe fourth table, `refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins`, stores information about which plugins are enabled for each user. Each row represents a user-plugin relationship, with columns for the user's ID, plugin name, position, and other relevant data.\nThe fifth table, `refinery_images`, stores information about images uploaded to the CMS. Each row represents an image, with columns for the image's ID, MIME type, name, size, width, height, and other relevant data.\nThe sixth table, `refinery_image_translations`, stores information about image translations. Each row represents an image translation, with columns for the image's ID, locale, created at, updated at, image alt, and image title.\nThe seventh table, `refinery_pages`, stores information about pages in the CMS. Each row represents a page, with columns for the page's ID, parent ID, path, show in menu, link URL, menu match, deletable, draft, skip to first child, LFT, RGT, depth, view template, layout template, created at, updated at, children count, and other relevant data.\nThe eighth table, `refinery_page_parts`, stores information about page parts in the CMS. Each row represents a page part, with columns for the page part's ID, page ID, slug, position, created at, updated at, title, and other relevant data.\nThe ninth table, `refinery_page_part_translations`, stores information about page part translations. Each row represents a page part translation, with columns for the page part's ID, locale, created at, updated at, body, and other relevant data.\nThe tenth table, `refinery_page_translations`, stores information about page translations. Each row represents a page translation, with columns for the page's ID, locale, created at, updated at, title, custom slug, menu title, slug, and other relevant data.\nThe eleventh table, `refinery_resources`, stores information about resources uploaded to the CMS. Each row represents a resource, with columns for the resource's ID, file MIME type, file name, file size, file UID, file ext, created at, and updated at.\nThe twelfth table, `refinery_resource_translations`, stores information about resource translations. Each row represents a resource translation, with columns for the resource's ID, resource title, locale, created at, updated at, and other relevant data.\nIn summary, this schema is used to store information about users, roles, images, pages, page parts, and resources in a Ruby on Rails application called Refinery. It uses a variety of tables and relationships to store and organize this information in a structured and efficient manner.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a content management system (CMS) tailored for Ruby on Rails developers. Refinery CMS is designed to create customizable and content-manageable websites efficiently by adhering to \"The Rails Way.\" It is well-suited for developers familiar with Ruby on Rails and aims to streamline the development process.\n\nObjectives\n\n- Provide an intuitive CMS for building and managing websites.\n- Simplify content creation and management with visual tools.\n- Support easy customization through extensions and plugins.\n- Facilitate secure user authentication and role management.\n- Enable seamless integration of media files and resources.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Primarily Ruby on Rails developers who will implement and customize websites using Refinery CMS.\n- Administrators: Users responsible for managing website content, structure, and user access.\n- End-users: Individuals who will interact with the front-end of websites built on Refinery CMS.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Page Management: \n   - Edit and organize pages using a visual editor.\n   - Manage site structure and navigation.\n\n2. Media Management:\n   - Upload and insert images seamlessly using Dragonfly.\n   - Store media on Amazon S3 for scalability.\n   - Manage and link to various resources such as PDF documents.\n\n3. User Authentication & Roles:\n   - Manage user access and roles using Devise.\n   - Define permissions for extensions and functionalities per user.\n\n4. Extension Support:\n   - Generate custom extensions using the Refinery extension generator.\n   - Popular extensions include:\n     - Blog: Manage posts, categories, and comments.\n     - Portfolio: Create image galleries.\n     - News: Post and manage news items.\n     - Inquiries: Handle contact form submissions and notifications.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ease of Use: Designed to be approachable for Ruby on Rails developers, leveraging Rails conventions.\n- Scalability: Supports scalable media storage with Amazon S3 integration.\n- Security: Secure authentication and role management using industry-standard practices (Devise).\n- Extensibility: Easily extensible through generators and available plugins.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0006.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0006\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `encrypted_password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_roles_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `plugin_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `plugin_name`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_authentication_devise_user_plugins_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_authentication_devise_users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_images` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `mime_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `width` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `height` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_image_translations` (\n  `image_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(6) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `image_alt` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`image_id`, `locale`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_image_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`image_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_images` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_pages` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `show_in_menu` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `link_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `menu_match` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deletable` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `draft` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `skip_to_first_child` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `lft` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rgt` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `depth` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `view_template` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `layout_template` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `children_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_pages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_parts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_parts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_part_translations` (\n  `page_part_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(6) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`page_part_id`, `locale`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_part_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_part_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_page_parts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_page_translations` (\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(6) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `custom_slug` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `menu_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`page_id`, `locale`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_page_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_pages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_resources` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `file_mime_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `file_uid` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_ext` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `refinery_resource_translations` (\n  `resource_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `resource_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(6) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`resource_id`, `locale`),\n  CONSTRAINT `refinery_resource_translations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`resource_id`) REFERENCES `refinery_resources` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
